[agent] I will now create a Databricks notebook to compute the recommendations. The notebook will:
[agent] 1. Load the user embeddings, item embeddings, and interactions.
[agent] 2. For each user, compute the dot product between their embedding and all item embeddings.
[agent] 3. Exclude items the user has already interacted with.
[agent] 4. Rank the top-5 items by dot product score, breaking ties by ascending `item_id`.
[agent] 5. Write the results to a feature table named `recse3a36e` in the specified schema.
[agent] 6. Enable low-latency lookup for the feature table.
